      "message": "**Unvalidated Span Sizes in `crypto_util.cc`** The `AesGcmEncrypt` and `AesGcmDecrypt` functions accept `std::span` arguments for keys, IVs, and tags, but they fail to validate the lengths of these spans before passing the underlying raw pointers to OpenSSL/BoringSSL.\n\n* **Vulnerability:** `EVP_aes_256_gcm()` strictly requires a 32-byte key. If a caller passes a smaller key span, `EVP_EncryptInit_ex` will perform an out-of-bounds read, potentially leading to a segfault or extracting arbitrary memory into the cipher state.  \n* **Remediation:** Add strict length validations at the beginning of these functions:\n\n```c\nif (key.size() !\u003d 32 || iv.size() !\u003d 12 || tag.size() !\u003d 16) {\n    return std::unexpected(CryptoError::kInvalidParam); // Add this error code\n}\n\n```",
