      "message": "Instead of using magic numbers, let\u0027s add constants. Here\u0027s Gemini-generated code to do this:\n\n---\n\n### **Feedback: Cryptographic Span Validation and Constant Ownership**\n\n**Rationale for the Change:**\n\n1. **Safety First (Out-of-Bounds Prevention):** The OpenSSL `EVP` functions require strictly sized buffers (e.g., exactly 32 bytes for an AES-256 key, 12 for the GCM IV, 16 for the tag). Because `std::span` erases compile-time length guarantees (unless explicitly typed as `std::span\u003cT, N\u003e`), passing an unvalidated dynamic span to the underlying C-API risks out-of-bounds reads or writes. We must validate lengths at the boundary.\n2. **Separation of Concerns:** Currently, the size constants for the AES-GCM IV and Tag live inside the `BootromComm` class, while the key size is hardcoded as `32`. These cryptographic parameters are inherent to the AES-GCM algorithm, not the Egis Bootrom protocol.\n3. **Single Source of Truth:** By moving these constants into the `crypto` namespace, `crypto_util` becomes fully self-contained and robust. `BootromComm` can then safely consume these constants, preventing \"magic numbers\" and ensuring everything stays perfectly aligned.\n\n---\n\n### **Implementation Instructions**\n\n#### **Step 1: Update `crypto_util.h**`\n\nDefine the cryptographic constants and add a new error code for invalid parameters.\n\n```cpp\n// In util/egis/crypto_util.h\n\nnamespace egis::crypto {\n\n// Add these constants\nconstexpr size_t kAes256KeySize \u003d 32;\nconstexpr size_t kAesGcmIvSize \u003d 12;\nconstexpr size_t kAesGcmTagSize \u003d 16;\n\nenum class CryptoError {\n  kContextAllocationFailed,\n  kInitFailed,\n  kUpdateFailed,\n  kFinalizeFailed,\n  kTagMismatch,\n  kRngFailed,\n  kInvalidParam, // \u003c-- Add this new error code\n};\n\n// ... existing code ...\n\n```\n\nDon\u0027t forget to update the `ToString(CryptoError err)` function in `crypto_util.h` to handle `CryptoError::kInvalidParam`!\n\n#### **Step 2: Add Validation to `crypto_util.cc**`\n\nEnforce the bounds at the very beginning of the AES-GCM functions.\n\n```cpp\n// In util/egis/crypto_util.cc\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, CryptoError\u003e AesGcmEncrypt(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e key, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e iv,\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e aad, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e plaintext,\n    std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e ciphertext, std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e tag) {\n    \n  // Add runtime bounds checking\n  if (key.size() !\u003d kAes256KeySize || iv.size() !\u003d kAesGcmIvSize || tag.size() !\u003d kAesGcmTagSize) {\n    return std::unexpected(CryptoError::kInvalidParam);\n  }\n\n  // ... rest of the function\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, CryptoError\u003e AesGcmDecrypt(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e key, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e iv,\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e aad, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e ciphertext,\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e tag, std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e plaintext) {\n    \n  // Add runtime bounds checking\n  if (key.size() !\u003d kAes256KeySize || iv.size() !\u003d kAesGcmIvSize || tag.size() !\u003d kAesGcmTagSize) {\n    return std::unexpected(CryptoError::kInvalidParam);\n  }\n\n  // ... rest of the function\n}\n\n```\n\n#### **Step 3: Refactor `bootrom.h` to consume the constants**\n\nRemove the local constants and update the structs and class members to use the new `crypto::` constants.\n\n```cpp\n// In util/egis/bootrom.h\n\n// 1. You will need to include the crypto header\n#include \"crypto_util.h\"\n\n// ... \n\nclass BootromComm {\n public:\n  static constexpr size_t kStatusHeaderSize \u003d 2;\n  static constexpr size_t kWrappedCommandSize \u003d 4;\n  // REMOVE: static constexpr size_t kAesGcmIvSize \u003d 12;\n  // REMOVE: static constexpr size_t kAesGcmTagSize \u003d 16;\n  static constexpr size_t kSha256DigestSize \u003d 32;\n  \n  // 2. Update the header size calculations\n  static constexpr size_t kScHeaderSizeSha \u003d\n      kStatusHeaderSize + kWrappedCommandSize + kSha256DigestSize;\n  static constexpr size_t kScHeaderSizeAes \u003d\n      kStatusHeaderSize + kWrappedCommandSize + crypto::kAesGcmIvSize + crypto::kAesGcmTagSize;\n\n  // 3. Update the struct array sizes\n  struct SecureCommandAesHeader {\n    uint8_t command_id \u003d EgisBootrom::kCmdSecureWrapped;\n    uint8_t algo;\n    uint32_t payload_len;\n    std::array\u003cuint8_t, crypto::kAesGcmIvSize\u003e iv{};\n    std::array\u003cuint8_t, crypto::kAesGcmTagSize\u003e tag{};\n  } __attribute__((packed));\n\n  // ...\n  \n  // 4. Update the SetAesKey signature\n  void SetAesKey(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t, crypto::kAes256KeySize\u003e key) {\n    std::copy(key.begin(), key.end(), aes_key_.begin());\n  }\n\n private:\n  EgisCryptoType wrapped_algo_ \u003d EgisCryptoType::kSha256;\n  \n  // 5. Update the member variable size\n  std::array\u003cuint8_t, crypto::kAes256KeySize\u003e aes_key_{};\n  \n// ...\n\n```\n\n#### **Step 4: Fix references in `bootrom.cc**`\n\nFinally, do a quick find-and-replace in `bootrom.cc` to fix any lingering references to the old constants.\n\nSpecifically, inside `BootromComm::SendBootromCommandAes`, you will need to change:\n\n* `BootromComm::kAesGcmIvSize`  $\\rightarrow$  `crypto::kAesGcmIvSize`\n* `BootromComm::kAesGcmTagSize` $\\rightarrow$  `crypto::kAesGcmTagSize`",
